# ─── Environments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Expo picks an env file by mode automatically — you don't switch by hand:
#
#   .env.development   → LOCAL Supabase.  Loaded by `expo start`.
#   .env.production    → CLOUD Supabase.  Loaded by production builds
#                        (eas build / expo export).
#   .env.*.local       → per-developer overrides (gitignored) — highest priority.
#
# Both .env.development and .env.production are committed: they hold only the
# public anon key (safe to ship — RLS protects the data), never the Gemini key,
# which lives only in the backend (petcare-backend) secrets.
#
# ─── Local dev ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `expo start` runs in development mode → uses .env.development → LOCAL Supabase.
# First start the backend:  cd ../petcare-backend && make dev
#
# 127.0.0.1 only reaches your Mac from the iOS Simulator. For a PHYSICAL DEVICE
# or the ANDROID EMULATOR, create .env.development.local (gitignored):
#
#   # physical device (same Wi-Fi as your Mac) — use your Mac's LAN IP:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:54321
#   # Android emulator:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:54321
#
# To dev against CLOUD instead (e.g. to test the tag finder flow on a real
# phone), put the .env.production values into .env.development.local.
#
# ─── Variables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# Finder web page (Vercel) the tag QR points to. Update after `vercel --prod`.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FINDER_BASE_URL=https://senly-finder.vercel.app
